Much effort is currently devoted to reducing ex vivo manipulation of CAR T cells\(^{51}\) to preserve their longevity and fitness, which are important factors for their antitumor activity\(^{52,53}\). Given the direct onset and fast decline of transposition, with a total absence of residual transposase \(72\,\mathrm{h}\) after transfection, SBprotAct is compatible with rapid cell manufacturing protocols. As primary T cells

are sensitive to transfection procedures, hsSB's cell-penetration property can further help reduce the number of transfection steps, simplify production and preserve cell fitness. Moreover, immunogenicity, which is caused by the presence of foreign protein or DNA, can lead to rejection of engineered cell grafts by the patient. Patient immune responses against CAR T cells have been observed
